 "language": "en",
 "text": "So here's the thing nobody tells you about the GTA 6 trailer. Everybody focused on the beach scene, but look at the top left corner. That timer is counting down from 47 seconds and it never resets. What if that's not a timer at all? What if it's a heist countdown? I went back through the 2025 footage frame by frame. And the biggest mistake people make is assuming it's pre rendered. It's actually running on the engine, you can see the draw distance pop. Here's why that matters for the release date. Rockstar never shows engine footage more than 18 months out. So the truth is, we're looking at a 2026 launch window, not 2027. Wait, it gets crazier. The map leak lines up perfectly with this shot. Listen, if you remember the 2022 leak, the airport was in the exact same spot. That's three independent sources pointing at the same thing. Insane. And nobody is talking about it. Drop a comment if you caught the second timer in the garage scene.",
